prompts.prompt:
Use case: ui-mockup. Create a polished ORIGINAL fantasy tactical-game ability-button concept sheet for a Chinese user, portrait 2:3, readable on a phone. This is a DESIGN SAMPLE, not game screenshot. The supplied reference is ONLY for column B semantic stone shapes and deeply CARVED numerals. Do not reproduce A/C columns or metal-inlaid numerals.
Title exactly "R2B · 01" and small subtitle "深凹刻 · 内敛魔力". Charcoal background, warm directional studio light from upper left, tactile sculpted grey basalt and restrained aged-brass rim, broad smooth readable faces, finely worn bevels. Not white flat text decals.
Layout: two LARGE complete circular skill controls stacked vertically, clearly separated. Each about 65% sheet width, with small labels to right. Below them a strip of THREE large shield stone material closeups. Keep all five stat badges close inside/on each button rim and inside its square bounding box; no spindly outlying indicators, no text overlaps. Center art upper portion; engraved Chinese ability name immediately beneath art within center lower portion. All names incised INTO a subtly lighter neutral stone plaque, no flat floating font. Give these centers enough empty margin.
UPPER SKILL: red rim and reddish-brown stone identity; central original painted illustration of a curved lightning boomerang, icon in the upper center, name EXACTLY "回旋镖" engraved underneath.
EXACT FIVE badge positions and values for upper button:
10 o'clock upper-left boot-shaped GREY stone, incised 4;
2 o'clock upper-right shield-shaped GREY stone, incised 3;
7:30 lower-left short wide sword-shaped muted RED stone, incised 3;
4:30 lower-right attack-distance muted RED stone: squat spearhead silhouette and a SMALL, unmistakable crosshair encircling a diagonal SPEAR in its upper carved portion, numeral 3 in separate lower recess;
6 o'clock bottom middle broad hourglass-shaped GREY stone, incised 9.
LOWER SKILL: blue rim. Upper center art shows an arcane hand levitating a small stone; Chinese name EXACTLY "控物" carved below.
EXACT FIVE badge positions for lower button:
10 o'clock GREY boot with incised 3;
2 o'clock GREY shield with incised 5;
7:30 lower-left BLUE primary-skill stone shaped like a broad arcane flame/hand crest with a carved hand/spell glyph and NO NUMERAL, not even 0;
4:30 lower-right BLUE circular range stone with a small TWO CONCENTRIC RINGS carved glyph in upper portion, carved 2 in separate lower recess;
6 o'clock GREY broad hourglass with incised 9.
Both skills same size and shared geometry language. Numerals are wide V-cut channels with shadowed recessed floors, lit cut walls and lighter worn bevels, unmistakably below the surface, readable neutral light stone from bevel light, never raised silver or gold metal characters. All other stats stay GREY irrespective of red/blue skill. ONLY primary lower-left and range/distance lower-right use card color. Do not tint upper shields or hourglass blue/red.
Right of upper button minimal caption "攻击距离" with thin line pointing to lower-right spear-crosshair badge. Right of lower button caption "技能范围" pointing to concentric-ring badge. No invented gameplay descriptions.
BOTTOM CLOSEUP STRIP: three identical GREY SHIELD-shaped stones, with deep numeral channels 6 / 8 / 4. Labels below "原值" / "增加" / "减少". First 6 unfilled dark cavity and pale bevel. Second 8 fills just the bottom of carved channels with controlled emerald GREEN magical liquid light; clearly recessed stone channel walls still visible. Third 4 same with ruby RED light. Only the NUMERAL recess glows, stone stays GREY. Soft local inner glow, no external sparks, flame or blown-out bloom. Tiny footer "概念样式 · 尚未实装". This footer and status values are material demonstrations. No glyph types swapped, no sixth badge, no initiative values outside hourglass, no brand logo, no unnecessary lettering. Keep shadows and material depth physically plausible; beautiful finished concept art suitable for later Blender translation.
